  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of winter assistance to vulnerable HH in Daikundi Province</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The 1st Standard Allocation allows Cordaid and OHW to provide the urgently needed winterization assistance to the most vulnerable people, extremely vulnerable families  having at least one person with special need. Daikundi is an isolated province with difficult terrain and poor access to main business centers of the country. The province is on the top of ICCT winter prioritization list, where vulnerable HHs are expected to face harsh winter with critical living conditions due to altitude, temperature, cold weather and lack of access to market during the winter.
During the winter season, most of the districts will have limited access to the main center or will be completely disconnected from the center of province. The province is agriculturally one of the least productive provinces as most of the land is barren and inaccessible with serious water shortages that cause extensive food insecurity. Due to Low economic conditions and lack of opportunities, there is a large percentage of person with disability and person with special need whose vulnerabilities have increased because of the difficult geography and being hard-to-reach area. Unemployment rate is very high, people have limited or no food stocks and are already relying on negative coping strategies for their survival. People cannot afford the cost of winterization materials and are in need of heating materials, warm clothing and blankets</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To save lives, reduce the suffering and improve the living conditions and dignity of most vulnerable people during winter by provision of seasonal winter assistance to the most vulnerable HHs in Daikundi Province</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Total 1550 individuals( 2079 Men, 2079 Women,3812 Boys and 3580 Girl</narrative>
  </description>
